  "contracts_and_consumers": [
    "Tutor request uses the existing ecological room/history/current-message/prior-mode builder and appends the selected active policy. It retains supported roles, inventory, checklist progress and verified assessment feedback supplied by the product.",
    "The parser independently validates reason-first v2 JSON, tutoring/Guard modes, allowed instructions and Guard-only null. It projects reason/decision/response into the existing TutorActionDecision without relabeling model decisions.",
    "Tutor truncated or malformed output gets at most one existing format repair at the same selected settings. Transport errors do not become ordinary suggestions; exhausted/invalid responses return success:false.",
    "RoomContext stores the parsed decision, reviewable learner-facing draft and effective config; human-reviewed send passes the raw decision and final mode through sendReviewedTutorResponse. Guard display and participation state derive from the persisted mode. The independent downstream suites exercise Guard recovery, refused delivery and explicit no-assessment routing to ordinary tutoring.",
    "Transfer analysis keeps the current persisted focus learner/message, complete supplied item and bounded dialogue history. It requests one item at a time, validates IDs, evidence quote, event kind/type and explanation, and preserves unsupported proposals as rejected_events. Actual progress eligibility remains enforced by the unchanged reducer and RPC.",
    "Transfer analysis precedes assessment eligibility/preparation. Assessment preparation, delivery, grading and public/private projection contracts remain unchanged; invalid/provider responses retain named failures. An ordinary learner message and an explicit assessment answer continue through distinct consumer paths."
